                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "98800edb-9ca0-4b49-bdd3-df5bb40af01f",
                        "source_entry_id": "4f796eae-3a89-30a6-912f-44458f558053",
                        "source_sense_id": "f55da538-21d1-3980-804a-37c656f4984c",
                        "target_lang_word": "reactionary",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "reactionary",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52c48873-b5d5-3a08-a151-c621b3ae5ad8",
                                        "entry_id": "d52b538f-5519-3187-9928-45c519ee6e3f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Extremely conservative; opposing revolution (such as the French Revolution); favoring a return to a golden age of the past."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c7b7681-431e-476d-9286-d8216846170a",
                                                "sense_id": "52c48873-b5d5-3a08-a151-c621b3ae5ad8",
                                                "text": "There's a fairly simple reason for the embrace of radicalism on the right, and it has to do with the reactionary imperative that lies at the core of conservative doctrine. […] If he is to preserve what he values, the conservative must declare war against the culture as it is."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52ac9d8e-6662-47d9-bda9-492e469e6ba4",
                                                "sense_id": "52c48873-b5d5-3a08-a151-c621b3ae5ad8",
                                                "text": "[Jeffrey] Epstein was interested in transhumanism, a theory of human perfection via technological manipulation that—like its predecessor, eugenics—is shot through with racist and reactionary ideas."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14240758-ac51-30b8-bf3a-66a5551a4c1f",
                                        "entry_id": "d52b538f-5519-3187-9928-45c519ee6e3f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, pertaining to, participating in, or inducing a chemical reaction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ea7c006-0300-47e2-95f3-42ba31bdf17c",
                                                "sense_id": "14240758-ac51-30b8-bf3a-66a5551a4c1f",
                                                "text": "Psychiatry extends the theory into biology in the belief that all human behavior is nothing more than a series of reactionary chemical processes in the brain that determine pre-coded genetic responses built up from the conditioning of one’s environment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fc0148a8-e1fa-33bd-b290-4d980c2d389a",
                                        "entry_id": "d52b538f-5519-3187-9928-45c519ee6e3f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In reaction to; as a result of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08465880-e9f8-49e0-a275-9b543a139efd",
                                                "sense_id": "fc0148a8-e1fa-33bd-b290-4d980c2d389a",
                                                "text": "The regulator noted that reduced service levels and passenger numbers helped deliver strong performance, with fewer reactionary delays."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "reactionary",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c64d8708-06e0-367b-80c2-4f3daf21ebc2",
                                        "entry_id": "6717d62e-dc4a-34b9-a994-f4fd45ea2196",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who opposes revolution, wanting to reverse it, favoring a return to a past golden age. Often used as a derogatory by revolutionaires."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a54872ea-2b98-44df-8978-eb296e5d8c71",
                                                "sense_id": "c64d8708-06e0-367b-80c2-4f3daf21ebc2",
                                                "text": "Hindu reactionaries, whose conception of a well-ordered society had not moved beyond the laws of Manu, fell into line for the moment with the intellectual products of the modern Indian University."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72b8800a-2375-4804-8171-0973a7a7069d",
                                                "sense_id": "c64d8708-06e0-367b-80c2-4f3daf21ebc2",
                                                "text": "It is not simply a conservative preference for things as they are, with a few nudges back, but a passionate loathing of the status quo and a desire to return to the past in one emotionally cathartic revolt. If conservatives are pessimistic, reactionaries are apocalyptic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3889396d-8b80-44f3-9118-8e46c29a5855",
                        "source_entry_id": "4f796eae-3a89-30a6-912f-44458f558053",
                        "source_sense_id": "f55da538-21d1-3980-804a-37c656f4984c",
                        "target_lang_word": "misoneism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "misoneism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "009f1803-ee67-34ca-9d35-91ea2fb5b71b",
                                        "entry_id": "296b234a-2938-3791-848f-3c41f3938be9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The distrust or hatred of new ideas or things."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "954ac402-53d0-44fe-a0ba-d2f77d122898",
                                                "sense_id": "009f1803-ee67-34ca-9d35-91ea2fb5b71b",
                                                "text": "In politics this type of philistine has more than once denounced the \"golden rule\" as an \"iridescent dream\" of a lunatic. Such philistinism pleases the misoneism of the mediocre, whence the enthusiasm over platitudes and the reign of the philistine in newspaper art, literature and science."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6a67cd9-fe1c-4cec-a242-75bae033d8a7",
                                                "sense_id": "009f1803-ee67-34ca-9d35-91ea2fb5b71b",
                                                "text": "Perché non mi adeguo all'introduzione di tali progressi anche nel calcolo delle probabilità, già universalmente accettata portando anche ivi grandiosi progressi? Si tratta di incomprensione? di misoneismo? di civetteria nel preferire utensili artigianali nell'era dell'automazione che permette la confezione in serie perfino di cervelli sia elettronici che umani?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56886947-b2f1-40c9-a3c4-a6741aaf6c6b",
                                                "sense_id": "009f1803-ee67-34ca-9d35-91ea2fb5b71b",
                                                "text": "What really got his attention was the Lombrosian concept of “misoneism”. Radicals, militants, revolutionaries, however they styled themselves, all sinned against this deep organic human principle, which Lombroso had named after the Greek for “hatred of anything new.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1bc7837f-4a10-44ff-94ac-d42760770b48",
                        "source_entry_id": "4f796eae-3a89-30a6-912f-44458f558053",
